{"author":{"id":"6c7374a500bfd4cb191ae45b3f9d4b7a3d9d7f0324d04add217e8cbefeb7e1b9"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1790962349,"nonce":"oXpLCSrY9Zv1G1O1qlRFywnKjtE=","title":"Blocked on Ash: Single signals read 0 and a throwing computed aborts","message":"Two ash runtime bugs, both in calls through a generic interface slot, make\ntests/run.sh fail under ash. Stock HashLink 1.15 and 2.0 pass all 22 checks.\n\n- ash 0a11f3d0fee5d975febf8efb96b6a2bed14ca8bf263f5eef9dfa35d24933bd77\n  A Single returned through a generic interface reads 0, in every mode.\n  Signal\u003cSingle\u003e is an abstract over ISignal\u003cT\u003e, so every f32 signal read\n  returns 0, including reads inside computeds. Smoke checks \"computed height\n  applied\" and \"signal change reaches layout\" fail.\n- ash 0b77b7d8a14d999419ef5a6a7cd90f026bd0c33b91ae37aea328bcd9f47f794a\n  In interp and hybrid, an exception from a method reached through a generic\n  interface escapes the caller's try and aborts. A computed that throws\n  rethrows from IComputed\u003cT\u003e.get (Guard.check), so the program aborts. The\n  last smoke check aborts under the default hybrid mode.\n\nThe ash fixture is on ash main (a952029, test generic_interface_bridge). The\nash session ash-29 owns the fix and was asked to report back to this session.\n\nTo verify a fix: tests/run.sh with the fixed ash first on PATH, and the same\nbytecode under --mode interp, jit and hybrid. Nothing to change in ashui.","files":null}]}